{
  "raw": {
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/South-Street-Campus/Aboriginal-and-Torres-Strait-Islander-Talent-Register_JR102224": {
      "title": "Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Talent Register",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-12-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nAbout Us Situated on Whadjuk and Binjareb Noongar lands, Murdoch University was founded over 40 years ago on principles of social inclusion, equity and free-thinking. Today, we remain a university for all, irrespective of social, cultural, or economic backgrounds. We invite you to help us achieve our goals – and yours – by registering your interest in career opportunities through our talent register. Join the team! Are you of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander heritage? Are you looking to advance your career in an inclusive and supportive atmosphere? We invite you to express your interest in joining our team. Current Murdoch students are especially encouraged to register.   Simply click ‘Apply’ to begin the process and submit your up-to-date resume. Next Steps! By registering, you will become part of our candidate pool and will be considered for current job openings. We are committed to increasing the representation of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander employees, your skills and experience may even lead to the creation of new positions. A member of our People and Culture team may contact you to discuss the types of opportunities you are interested in. Registration on the talent register does not guarantee an employment offer, however it can make it easier for you to be considered for future positions. Prior to any placements, regular selection and screening processes will apply in line with our Recruitment Policy. Questions? We’re here to help! If you have any queries please reach out to our Senior Advisor First Nations - Allana Sheppard at Allana.Sheppard@murdoch.edu.au Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Veterinary-Nurse--ECC-_JR105803": {
      "title": "Veterinary Nurse (ECC)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout The Team The Emergency and Critical Care/Intensive Care Unit service provides high-quality emergency, critical care and intensive nursing support for small animal patients requiring urgent assessment, close monitoring, advanced treatment and ongoing hospital care. Working alongside clinicians, specialists, residents, interns and the broader hospital team, our ECC/ICU nurses play a key role in patient stabilisation, monitoring, treatment delivery and continuity of care across the hospital. You would be joining a collaborative and supportive team within a busy teaching hospital environment. Your New Role!   The key purpose of this role is to provide high-quality emergency, critical care and intensive veterinary nursing care to animals in The Animal Hospital at Murdoch University. Your Key responsibilities will include – Provide all aspects of veterinary nursing care as per the Certificate IV of Veterinary Nursing and the Prescribed Duties of Veterinary Nurses within the Vet Surgeons Act of WA. Comply with University and TAHMU policies, procedures and protocols. Comply with The Veterinary Surgeons’ Act of WA and other veterinary industry related Acts and Regulations. Liaise with clinical areas within the hospital to coordinate daily availability of equipment and technical support. Assist clinicians with examinations, workups, procedures, treatments and surgeries. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (12 Month) | Part time  (up to 30 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $74,809K – $79,802K (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions, with the option to sacrifice 5% of your superannuation into your salary.    We are committed to supporting the growth and wellbeing of our team members through a comprehensive professional development program both external and internal, including: Generous Continuing Professional Development (CPD) allowance Access to RECOVER Certification and Training to develop advanced CPR and emergency response skills Australian Veterinary Association (AVA) Membership supported by the hospital Access to @Dove resources and wellbeing programs to support personal and professional resilience Ongoing mentorship from ECC clinicians, specialists, and senior nursing staff Opportunities to develop advanced ECC nursing skills Exposure to a diverse and challenging referral caseload Supportive team culture focused on learning, collaboration, and excellence in patient care Employee assistance and wellbeing initiatives You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Completion of a Certificate IV in Veterinary Nursing or equivalent, or completion of a relevant Veterinary Nursing Diploma level qualification registrable in Western Australia. Ability to work outside of normal business hours, including rotational shift work, weekends and public holidays Demonstrated confidence and skill when handling and restraining small animals. Excellent organisational, time and workload management skills, including the ability to prioritise workload to meet strict deadlines. Highly effective communication, customer service and interpersonal skills, and the demonstrated ability to interact constructively and collaboratively with staff at all levels of the organisation. Demonstrated ability to use initiative, assume responsibility for tasks and projects and to resolve problems. Proven ability to work independently as well as fitting seamlessly into a team environment. Minimum of 2 years of experience in a clinical and/or emergency setting Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Joey Rideout, ECC Supervisor,   joey.rideout@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105803 as the reference. Applications Close on 18th September 2026(11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Facilities-Services-Officer_JR105739": {
      "title": "Facilities Services Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The Campus Development portfolio delivers infrastructure, maintenance and capital projects that support the University's growth, sustainability and long-term strategic goals, creating environments that enable learning, research and community engagement. Your New Role!   The Facilities Services Officer provides frontline customer service and administrative support for Campus Development and Facilities Maintenance. Based at the University's service centre, the role coordinates maintenance requests, service enquiries and contractor activities across areas including facilities, security, parking, grounds, cleaning and logistics. The position also supports contractor compliance processes, inductions, permits and work order administration across all campuses. Your Key responsibilities will include – Communicate directly with customers, contractors and internal personnel to streamline and optimise the logging, assignment, scheduling and follow-up of outstanding work requests Provide a high-quality reception service to external and internal customers in Facilities Management and Campus Development, acting as a central point of contact for the University while maintaining professionalism and customer service excellence Receive and manage service requests and maintenance tickets through the University’s maintenance management system, raising and administering work orders as required, and working collaboratively with the Business Support team and service providers to support the delivery, completion and administrative close-out of maintenance works Evaluate critical service interruptions and communicate them clearly to the broader University and relevant stakeholders through intranet notifications, alert banners and email communications, ensuring timely dissemination of important information. Ensure contractors remain administratively compliant with Murdoch working guidelines and regulations, including maintaining and auditing the electronic attendance register, managing contractor inductions, updating the Contractor Management Presentation Induction and facilitating high-risk permit-to-work applications. Provide sound advice and clear explanations in relation to contractor management administration, relevant guidelines and associated Murdoch regulations. Act as custodian of the key management system and automated KeyWatcher cabinet, including governance of high-risk keys, access cards, audits, reporting, key reservations and authorisations. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Continuous, Full Time attracts a remuneration of $74,809 – $91,567 plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Completion of a Certificate IV qualification with relevant Facilities Management work experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant work experience and education/training. Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and database-style software to convey information and maintain accurate records. Ability to be self-organised and manage time effectively, including prioritising workloads to meet deadlines and competing records. Highly effective communication, customer service and interpersonal skills, with demonstrated ability to interact constructively and collaboratively with the University community. Proven ability to enter data accurately and produce basic reports for management use in measuring performance against service KPIs. Demonstrated ability to use initiative, take responsibility for tasks and solve problems effectively. Ability to work effectively and autonomously in a small, busy team environment. Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Carola Schwan, Business Manager Campus Development and quote JR105739 as the reference. Applications Close on 18th September 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
