    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Associate-Professor-in-Small-Animal-Surgery_JR105260": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer or Associate Professor in Small Animal Surgery",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team Our Small Animal Surgery team provides specialist referral services across soft tissue, oncologic, orthopaedic and neurosurgical cases. Due to the upcoming retirement of one of our long-standing Professors, we have two positions available in our surgery team for either Soft Tissue or Orthopaedics focussed or someone who enjoys all aspects of surgery. The team consisting of two board certified surgeons, one residency trained surgeon, three residents and two Post Graduate Trainees (interns) brings together extensive surgical expertise to support pets with a wide range of complex conditions, from abdominal, thoracic and cardiovascular procedures through to advanced orthopaedic, spinal and reconstructive surgery. Working within a fully equipped hospital environment, the team is supported by specialist anaesthesia, 24-hour intensive care, internal medicine, oncology, cardiology, advanced diagnostic imaging, clinical pathology laboratory and highly skilled nursing staff. This integrated approach allows the service to manage challenging surgical cases while maintaining a high standard of care before, during and after surgery. The team works closely with referring veterinarians to provide advice, consultation and surgical treatment tailored to each patient’s needs. Whether a case is straightforward or highly complex, their focus is on delivering expert surgical care and supporting a smooth recovery through coordinated postoperative management with the pet’s regular veterinarian. Your New Role!   The Animal Hospital at Murdoch University stands out as a leading veterinary centre in Western Australia, offering a diverse caseload, advanced diagnostic facilities, and a collaborative environment. As part of a prestigious university, you’ll work alongside world-class specialists and contribute to teaching and research, ensuring continual professional growth. Our commitment to excellence, innovation, and compassionate care creates a unique learning culture where both new graduates and experienced veterinarians thrive. You’ll join a supportive, friendly team dedicated to clinical excellence and personal wellbeing. We provide structured mentorship programs, ongoing training, and opportunities to participate in groundbreaking research. Competitive compensation and a strong focus on professional development make The Animal Hospital at Murdoch University an ideal workplace for passionate veterinary professionals seeking both career advancement and community. Position Descriptions Senior Lecturer Associate Professor What We Offer You! Renumeration, Visa Sponsorship and Relocation is negotiable. You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: A degree in Veterinary Science registrable with the Veterinary Surgeons’ Board of Western Australia A clinical specialist qualification (DECVS, DACVS or fellowship) in small animal surgery. Demonstrated ability to work under broad direction only, exercise initiative in undertaking responsibilities and work effectively as a team member. A high level of achievement in successfully supervising honours, Masters by Coursework, HDR and postgraduate students (including residents) to completion. A record of success in the application of curriculum design and pedagogy, including substantial experience with leading and designing programs of study. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Visa sponsorship and relocation may be available for the right candidate. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Henry Annandale, Dean of Veterinary Medicine, henry.annandale@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105260 as the reference. Applications Close on 16 October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Agricultural-Science-Teaching-and-Learning-Talent-Register_JR105577": {
      "title": "Agricultural Science Teaching and Learning Talent Register",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nAbout The Team The School of Agricultural Science at Murdoch University is shaping the future of agriculture through excellence in teaching, research and industry engagement. Our teaching and learning activities prepare graduates to address challenges in food and fibre production, animal health and biosecurity. We deliver undergraduate and postgraduate degrees, together with research training programs. Our coursework offerings include majors in: Animal Science Animal Health Crop and Pasture Science Biosecurity Food Security The team also delivers minors in Equine Science and Agribusiness. Our teaching and learning programs combine strong foundational knowledge with hands-on learning through laboratories, fieldwork and industry placements, equipping students with the skills and networks needed for careers in modern agriculture, animal health and biosecurity. About the opportunity We invite expressions of interest from candidates with relevant academic and/or industry experience to join our teaching talent register for casual and fixed-term opportunities within the School of Agricultural Science. Lectures Workshops, laboratory classes and field-based teaching activities Tutorials Marking Animal handling demonstration involving horses, cattle, sheep and pigs We welcome applications from both experienced educators and industry professionals who can bring contemporary knowledge and real-world perspectives to student learning. Please register for the talent pool online via the Apply Now button. The following documents should be submitted to support your application: A cover letter that includes: an outline of your areas of expertise and relevant experience subject areas and teaching activities of interest availability for face-to-face teaching at the Murdoch University South Street Campus and/or online delivery Your most recent resume (CV) detailing academic qualifications, teaching experience and relevant professional industry experience This Talent Register will remain active until 31st August 2027 Candidates whose skills and experience align with emerging teaching needs may be considered for casual or fixed-term teaching opportunities as they arise. Please note: successful candidates may be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Visa sponsorship is not available for positions that will be filled from this talent register. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity please reach out to agscience@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105577 as the reference. Applications for this talent register close on 31 August 2027 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Dubai/Academic-Opportunities-at-Murdoch-University-Dubai_JR105796": {
      "title": "Academic Opportunities at Murdoch University Dubai",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin a growing Australian university branch campus in one of the world’s most dynamic education hubs!   About Our Dubai Campus !     Murdoch University Dubai is the vibrant branch campus of Murdoch University, based in Perth, Australia. Home to a diverse community of over 1, 3 00 students, our campus offers a wide range of internationally recognised undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Located in the heart of Dubai’s thriving education hub, we combine global academic standards with local relevance, fostering an inclusive and innovative learning environment.   Murdoch University Dubai is building on its reputation in the region and is focused on growth, research and innovation and high-quality student outcomes. The campus offers a collaborative academic environment, modern teaching and learning facilities, and the opportunity to contribute to an Australian university with a global outlook.     Your New Role!   Murdoch University Dubai is inviting applications for six academic leadership positions ( refer to the attached D uty S tatements for role-specific responsibilities ) :   Discipline Lead – Psychology & Criminology   Discipline Lead – Business   Discipline Lead – Education   Subject Lead – AI & Data Science   Subject Lead – Cyber Security & Comput er Science   Subject Lead – Accounting & Finance   The roles offer an exciting opportunity to contribute to the next stage of growth for Murdoch University’s branch campus in Dubai, United Arab Emirates.   We are seeking talented, student-centred academics to join our collegial and growing campus community. Successful candidates will be appointed to an academic position at a level commensurate with their qualifications, experience, academic standing and discipline requirements, ranging from Lecturer (AU) / Ass istant Professor (US) to Professor (AU) / Full Professor, Senior Distinguished Level (US) .   As a member of our academic team, you will deliver high-quality teaching, support student success, contribute to curriculum development and academic quality, and engage in research and scholarly activity aligned with Murdoch University’s standards and strategic priorities.   These are academic appointments with responsibilities across both teaching and research. The role will involve curriculum delivery, unit coordination, assessment and moderation, student consultation and supervision, participation in academic governance and quality processes, industry engagement, and scholarly or research activity appropriate to the level of appointment.     Applicants should review both:   The relevant Duty Statement , which outlines the leadership responsibilities and role-specific requirements of the advertised position.   The Academic Position Description , which outlines the teaching, research, service and academic expectations associated with the level of appointment.     Academic Position Descriptions   Lecturer (AU) / Assistant Professor (US)   Senior Lecturer (AU) / Associate Professor (US)   Associate Professor (AU) / Professor - Full Professor (US)   Professor (AU) / Full Professor Senior - Distinguished Level (US)     What We Offer You!   This is an opportunity to join a campus with momentum. For academics who enjoy teaching, curriculum development, student engagement, and the practical application of research and scholarship, these roles offer a unique opportunity to shape the learning experiences of students in Dubai while remaining connected to Murdoch University’s broader academic community in Western Australia and across its global network.   These positions are offered as fixed-term, full-time appointments for an initial three-year term . The nominal workload profile is expected to be approximately 85% teaching / service/ leadership and 15% research , providing a strong focus on teaching while supporting ongoing research, scholarship, and professional contribution.   22 days annual holiday leave , plus public holidays   Travel allowance - for employee and up to 3 eligible dependent family members   Private health insurance – for employee and up to 3 eligible dependent family members   Child e ducation allowance - for up to 2 dependen ts   Access to research opportunities     What you’ll bring to the role   Depending on the level of appointment, applicants will be expected to demonstrate an appropriate combination of:   Relevant disciplinary expertise and academic qualifications appropriate to the level of appointment.   Higher education teaching experience, including curriculum delivery, assessment and moderation capability.   Research, scholarly activity and/or professional contribution appropriate to discipline and career stage.   Industry, professional or community engagement relevant to the discipline area.   Academic coordination, governance, leadership or quality assurance experience, where relevant to the level of appointment.   A commitment to excellent teaching, student learning and student success.   The ability to work effectively in a diverse, multicultural and transnational education environment.   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application -    Your most recent resume (CV)     A brief cover letter outlining your discipline area, academic level sought , teaching experience, research or scholarly contribution, and leadership experience.     Applications submitted by post or email will not be accepted . Visa sponsorship and relocation are available .   Please see the Applicant Guide   for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunit ies on offer please reach out to Professor Michael Gallimore, Dean and Academic President of Dubai, Michael.Gallimore@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR 105796 as the reference.   Applications Close on 1 8 September 2026 (11.59pm AWST )   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Interviews may be scheduled upon application during the advertising period.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce.   Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Senior-Cyber-Operations-Analyst_JR105766": {
      "title": "Senior Cyber Operations Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The Cyber Security Team is at the forefront of protecting Murdoch University's digital landscape. The team is responsible for monitoring security threats, responding to incidents, managing cyber security technologies and driving continuous improvements to security practices across the University. With a strong focus on collaboration, innovation and resilience, the team works together to address emerging cyber risks while supporting the University's strategic goals. It's an environment where curiosity, problem-solving and continuous learning are encouraged, providing opportunities to make a meaningful impact every day. Your New Role!   As the Senior Cyber Operations Analyst, you'll be a key member of the Cyber Security Team, helping to protect and strengthen Murdoch University's digital environment. You'll provide technical leadership across security operations, driving improvements to security technologies, detecting and responding to cyber threats, and leading investigations into complex security incidents. Working closely with the Cyber Operations Lead and stakeholders across the University, you'll identify security risks, implement solutions, and help shape the University's cyber security capability. You'll also mentor team members, champion best practice, and contribute to a culture of continuous improvement and innovation. Your Key Responsibilities will include: Lead the management and continuous improvement of cyber security technologies and controls. Monitor, investigate, and respond to cyber security threats and incidents. Identify security gaps and drive remediation initiatives to strengthen the University's security posture. Act as a technical escalation point for complex security investigations and incidents. Provide expert advice on security technologies, processes, and best practices. Mentor team members and support the ongoing development of team capability. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (12 Months) | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $116K – $133K (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: A degree in Cyber Security, Information Technology, or a related discipline, or equivalent experience gained through professional practice and training. Experience working with a range of cyber security technologies, including endpoint protection, SIEM platforms, vulnerability management tools, firewalls, and networking solutions. A solid understanding of security incident response, with the ability to investigate, analyse and resolve complex security issues. Strong knowledge of Microsoft Defender technologies, particularly Defender for Endpoint or similar endpoint security solutions. Experience using Microsoft Purview, scripting, and KQL to support security monitoring, investigation and governance activities. Analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify root causes and implement effective solutions. Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Alan Fereday, Head of IT Operations, alan.fereday@murdoch.edu.au and quote in the subject line JR105766 as the reference . Applications Close on 22 September 2026 11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Veterinarian_JR105824": {
      "title": "Veterinarian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nEmergency and Critical Care specialists provide a trainee and residency program along with training and guidance opportunities for the emergency team members. The hospital also receives afterhours support from various specialist services to ensure optimal care and treatment plans for all animals. Your New Role!   The key purpose of this role is to provide emergency veterinary services and ongoing care for companion animals (including exotics) in the Emergency and Critical Care section of The Animal Hospital at Murdoch University (TAHMU). Your Key responsibilities will include – Diagnose and make therapeutic treatment recommendations on small companion animals. Provide support and training to specialty trainees, students, visiting veterinarians and veterinary nurses in all aspects of emergency medicine and critical care. Provide advice to other TAHMU staff on emergency medicine and critical care related matters. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This casual role attracts a competitive base casual rate of $74.55p/hr – $85.33 p/hr PLUS shift penalties and 12% employer superannuation contributions.  Shift Penalties Midweek 18:00 – 23:59 Hours – Attracts 115% penalty on base hourly rate - $79.60 p/h - $90.38 p/h Midweek 24:00 – 08:00 Hours – Attracts 130% penalty on base hourly rate - $96.92 p/h - $110.93 p/h Midweek O/night Shift – Attracts 150% penalty on base hourly rate - $111.83 p/h -128.00 p/h Saturday Hours – attracts 150% penalty on base hourly rate - $111.83 p/h -$128.00 p/h Sunday Hours – Attracts 175% penalty on base hourly rate  - $130.46 p/h - $149.33 p/h Public Holiday Hours – Attracts 250% penalty on base hourly rate - $186.38 p/h - $213.33 p/h You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Bronze- tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter that includes a statement addressing the selection criteria noted below to allow us to assess your suitability for this role. Your most recent resume (CV) Selection Criteria: Veterinary degree registrable by the Veterinary Practice Board of Western Australia. Relevant post graduate qualifications or training experience Ability to work rotational shift work, including night shifts, weekends and public holidays, and be flexible in work hour patterns. Demonstrated ability to work cohesively in a team environment. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Dr Joey Rideout, ECC Veterinary Supervisor, joey.rideout@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105824 as the reference. Applications Close on 4th October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Veterinary-Nurse_JR105817": {
      "title": "Veterinary Nurse (Large Animal)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team Murdoch University is home to the only Veterinary School in Western Australia, and its prestigious teaching hospital provides the clinical facility that enables students to have the clinical ‘hands-on’ opportunity. It also provides a service to community through its team of top specialists who oversee the care and treatment of all animals referred to the Hospital. The Animal Hospital at Murdoch University (TAHMU) aims to provide an environment where high professional and clinical standards, based on available scientific evidence, are tempered with genuine care and compassion. Your New Role!   You will be providing high quality veterinary nursing care to animals in The Animal Hospital at Murdoch University. Your Key responsibilities will include – Clinical Support: Provide nursing care for large animal patients, assist with procedures and surgeries, and triage cases to ensure timely treatment Operational Oversight: Maintain infection control, manage equipment and stock, ensure compliance with regulations, and keep accurate records Training and Communication: Supervise students in clinical techniques and communicate effectively with clients, veterinarians, and hospital staff Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (12 Months), with opportunity to extend, if the business requires it | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $74,809.00– $82,011.00 (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Generous Continuing Professional Development (CPD) allowance Australian Veterinary Association (AVA) Membership supported by the hospital Ongoing mentorship from specialists and senior nursing staff Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role  Indigenous Language Allowance   Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit  Employee Assistance Program  On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic  For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Certificate IV or Diploma in Veterinary Nursing (registrable in WA) Confident in handling and restraining large animals, including but not limited to racehorses, performance horses, foals, farm animals and those cheeky little ponies! Knowledge of diagnostic and surgical equipment, sterilisation, and aseptic techniques Proven ability to work independently and in teams, take initiative, and adapt to rotating shifts Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a collaborative approach to clients and colleagues, and the ability to manage all aspects of the Large Animal reception. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Mikaela Deetman, Nurse Supervisor, m.deetman@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105817 as the reference. Applications Close on 25th September 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
