    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Clinical-Training-Programs---School-of-Veterinary-Medicine_JR105823-1": {
      "title": "Clinical Training Programs - School of Veterinary Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\n\nMurdoch University School of Veterinary Medicine Clinical Training Programs commencing January 2027 The School of Veterinary Medicine, Murdoch University has vacancies in the following programs commencing in January 2027. 12-month discipline-specific traineeships Large Animal - Equine Small Animal Surgery Small Animal Rotating (Medicine, Oncology & Cardiology) Emergency & Critical Care Anaesthesia The 12-month postgraduate trainee program is a year-long, advanced clinical training program in the School of Veterinary Medicine at Murdoch University in Western Australia. The training program offers clinical experience in specific disciplines and an opportunity to gain formal scholarly training through concurrent enrolment in a graduate program. These positions would suit a recent graduate veterinarian interested in further university training and upskilling in areas relevant to general practice, or as a stepping stone to further clinical training, such as a residency. Exceptional new graduates will be considered. An annual stipend of $40k is offered with concurrent enrolment in the graduate program which results in award of a Graduate Diploma in Veterinary Clinical Studies after completion of 2 semesters. After-hours payments for relevant disciplines average between $10-20k per 12 months. Course fees are paid by the School (value approximately $20k). Residency training programs Anaesthesia x 2 Emergency & Critical Care Diagnostic Imaging Further resident programs will be advertised within the next few weeks – keep an eye out ! The three-year, full-time residency programs allow a successful candidate to target credential requirements for speciality certification. The residencies are supervised by board-certified academic staff. Concurrent part-time enrolment in a research master’s degree is required. Residents are employed as 0.8 FTE Associate Lecturer, with all of the benefits of a salaried staff member, including 17% employer superannuation contributions. Our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Salary packaging options – such as gym membership, car parking permits Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic Application process Applicants must be able to start the program in late July for Semester 2, 2026 enrolment. Application for clinical training positions is restricted to veterinarians with a degree that can be registered in Western Australia. Australian and New Zealand citizenship or Australian permanent residency status is required. All enquiries around the program can be forwarded to Jody Reeve by email: Jody.Reeve@murdoch.edu.au Applications close Sunday 20th September 2026 . ( Early applications/expressions of interest are encouraged) A letter of intent, current CV, certified copy of academic transcripts, names of 3 referees, and a certified copy of passport/visa as proof of Australian Citizenship or Permanent Residency, or of New Zealand citizenship, should be submitted to Jody.Reeve@murdoch.edu.au . Candidates are chosen after a competitive selection process. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Veterinary-Nurse_JR105811": {
      "title": "Veterinary Nurse",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The small animal surgery referral service offers specialty services in both soft tissue and oncologic surgery, and orthopaedic and neurosurgery. Our full range of facilities and state of the art surgical equipment, coupled with integrated support from specialist level care in anaesthesia, 24h intensive care, internal medicine, advanced diagnostic imaging and excellent nursing standards enable us to manage the most complex surgical challenges and ensure that our patients receive a very high standard of care across all aspects of surgical management. You would be joining a team of 7 veterinary nurses; the service is open to clientele 08:00 -18:00 Weekdays. Your New Role!   The key purpose of this role is to provide high quality veterinary nursing care to animals in The Animal Hospital At Murdoch University. Your Key responsibilities will include – Provide all aspects of veterinary nursing care as per the Certificate IV of Veterinary Nursing and the Prescribed Duties of Veterinary Nurses within the Vet Surgeons Act of WA. Comply with University and TAHMU policies, procedures and protocols. Comply with The Veterinary Surgeons’ Act of WA and other veterinary industry related Acts and Regulations. Liaise with clinical areas within the hospital to coordinate daily availability of equipment and technical support. Assist clinicians with examinations, workups, procedures, treatments and surgeries. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (12 Month) | Part time or Full Time (up to 37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $74,809K – $79,802K (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions, with the option to sacrifice 5% of your superannuation into your salary.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Completion of a Certificate IV in Veterinary Nursing or equivalent, or completion of a relevant Veterinary Nursing Diploma level qualification registrable in Western Australia. Demonstrated confidence and skill when handling and restraining small animals. Excellent knowledge of diagnostic and surgical equipment as well as sterilising and aseptic techniques. Demonstrated experience and exposure to various surgical procedures and patient care in a general practice setting. Excellent organisational, time and workload management skills, including the ability to prioritise workload to meet strict deadlines. Highly effective communication, customer service and interpersonal skills, and the demonstrated ability to interact constructively and collaboratively with staff at all levels of the organisation. Demonstrated ability to use initiative, assume responsibility for tasks and projects and to resolve problems. Proven ability to work independently as well as fitting seamlessly into a team environment. A strong interest in developing skills within a specialised area. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Dee Marchesi, Associate Clinical Director and Operations Manager,   d.marchesi@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105811 as the reference. Applications Close on 25th September 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Manager-Policy-Projects_JR105814": {
      "title": "Manager Policy Projects",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team Join the Office of Quality and Standards, a collaborative and supportive team dedicated to advancing academic excellence across the University. Working closely with colleagues throughout the university, we provide expert advice and support in academic policy, quality assurance, compliance, curriculum management, academic governance and student integrity. Together, we drive continuous improvement, support strategic initiatives and help ensure the University maintains high academic standards while meeting its regulatory obligations. Your New Role!   The Manager, Policy Projects is responsible for leading priority policy development and review initiatives that support the University's higher education provider reregistration program. Working closely with the Director, Quality and Standards and senior stakeholders across the University, you will translate regulatory, governance and operational requirements into clear, practical and implementable policy solutions. You will lead complex policy projects from design and consultation to approval, coordinating priorities, stakeholder engagement, and project delivery to ensure high-quality outcomes are achieved within agreed timeframes. The role plays an important part in strengthening institutional assurance and supporting the University's readiness for external review, with a primary focus on academic policy and opportunities to contribute to broader University policy initiatives. Key Responsibilities Lead priority policy development and review projects that support the University's reregistration program and strategic objectives. Develop and review policies, procedures, and related governance documents that align with regulatory and operational requirements. Manage project delivery, including planning, stakeholder consultation, risk management, reporting, and the coordination of priorities and timelines. Provide strategic policy advice and lead a small team to deliver high-quality, evidence-informed policy outcomes. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (to December 2027) | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) role attracts a remuneration of $134K – $140K plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: A degree with extensive relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education and training. Experience leading complex policy development or review projects within a large and complex organisation, ideally within the higher education sector. Exceptional written communication skills, with the ability to develop clear, concise and practical policies, procedures and business documentation. Strong project management skills, including the ability to manage plans, timelines, risks, stakeholder engagement and reporting across multiple priorities. Ability to interpret regulatory, governance and operational requirements and translate them into effective, implementable policy solutions. Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Verity Morgan, Director of Quality and Standards and University Secretary, verity.morgan@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105814 as the reference. Applications Close on 29 September 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Senior-Operations-Officer_JR105842": {
      "title": "Senior Operations Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team College Operations provides comprehensive academic and administrative support across all disciplines within the Colleges. It is a focused, multi-skilled, and digitally capable team that delivers high-quality technical, operational, project, event, and general support services to academics and researchers. Through this work, College Operations enables Murdoch University to successfully achieve its three core activities: Education, Research, and Engagement. Your New Role!   As part of the College Operations team supporting the College of Business, the Senior Operations Officer is responsible for supporting and maintaining the Colleges’ academic operations and student experience. The Senior Operations Officer provides a thorough and effective administrative support service for research, teaching and workload functions within the Colleges. This role involves collaborating with multiple departments to enhance service delivery. The Senior Operations Officer will provide leadership, supervision, and support to the College Operations Team and serve as a delegate for the College Business Manager when needed. Your Key responsibilities will include – Serve as the primary point of contact for Operations Officers, ensuring clear communication and timely support Provide expert subject‑matter guidance to strengthen operational decision‑making across the team Lead and manage both operational and strategic projects that drive the college’s priorities forward Foster a positive, solutions‑focused, and results‑driven culture through proactive leadership Oversee people administration, including recruitment coordination, onboarding, timesheet processing, and staff exits. Manage financial processes such as purchasing, reimbursements, and purchase orders. Provide governance support for committees, including agenda preparation and meeting documentation. Act as a key liaison between Colleges, Schools, and University departments. Drive continuous improvement and ensure compliance with policies and procedures. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (24 months with potential opportunity for extension), Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $82,210 – $100,496 (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What You’ll bring to the role: Completion of a diploma with subsequent relevant experience or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. Strong analytical capability, with experience using data and insights to improve processes, solve problems, and drive operational outcomes. Experience in academic or business operational support or office administration. Demonstrated high level of organisational, time and workload management skills, including the ability to prioritise workload to meet strict deadlines Experience in people leadership and development, with proven skills to motivate, inspire, and mobilise teams to foster a positive workplace culture and achieve high quality outcomes Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia.   Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Jordan Muir, College Business Manager and quote JR105842 a s the reference. Applications Close on 2nd October 2026 (11.59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
