    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Peel-WA/Lecturer-of-Nursing_JR105180": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer or Lecturer in Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The School of Nursing is a highly engaged, supportive and innovative academic team within the College of Health and Education. Our collegial culture is underpinned by a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, research and professional practice, with many team members recognised through national, state, university and industry awards. Working closely with extensive clinical partners and active national and international research collaborators, the Nursing team provides high-quality, student-focused learning experiences across undergraduate, postgraduate and research programs. Your New Role!   We are seeking two Associate Lecturers or Lecturers in Nursing to join our team. These positions are primarily based at our South Street campus in Murdoch; however, the successful applicants will also be required to teach at our Mandurah campus, with time allocated across both locations in line with teaching and operational requirements. As an Associate Lecturer , you will contribute to teaching, research and service within the School of Nursing while developing your academic profile under the guidance of senior academics. Key responsibilities: Deliver high-quality teaching across Nursing programs and campuses as required. Contribute to nursing research and scholarly outputs. Engage with the School, College, University and nursing profession. Work collaboratively across diverse healthcare and educational settings. As a Lecturer , you will undertake independent teaching, research and scholarly activity, making a significant contribution through your professional expertise and academic leadership. Key responsibilities: Deliver high-quality teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate Nursing programs. Conduct and lead nursing research, producing high-quality scholarly outputs. Engage with the School, College, University and nursing profession. Contribute to the coordination and leadership of academic activities. Work collaboratively across diverse healthcare and educational settings. Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement below for each role. Associate Lecturer Lecturer What We Offer You! This Continuous | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of: Associate Lecturer $81,513 – $109,925 (pro rata) Lecturer $115,512 – $136,831 (pro rata) Plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria and qualification requirement(s) (Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Associate Lecturer A degree in Nursing and a relevant postgraduate qualification at AQF Level 8 or above (or equivalent professional experience recognised by the University). Progress towards a higher degree, such as a PhD, is desirable. Current unrestricted AHPRA registration as a Registered Nurse. Ability to deliver evidence-based teaching using contemporary nursing education practices. Experience in nursing education with positive student outcomes. Experience contributing to curriculum development and quality teaching initiatives. Lecturer A PhD in Nursing or a related discipline (or equivalent professional experience). Current unrestricted AHPRA registration as a Registered Nurse. Experience delivering high-quality teaching and applying contemporary nursing education practices. Experience in nursing education with positive student outcomes. Ability to contribute to curriculum development, teaching excellence and educational innovation. Applicants should refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia.  Relocation may be available for the right candidate. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Frank Donnelly, Dean of Nursing, frank.donnelly@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105180 as the reference. Applications Close on 18 October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Learning-Accessibility-Consultant_JR105833": {
      "title": "Learning Accessibility Consultant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team Join a passionate and purpose-driven team dedicated to enhancing student wellbeing, inclusion and success. In Access, Wellbeing & Equity (AWE), you'll have the opportunity to make a meaningful difference by supporting students to overcome barriers, thrive in their studies and reach their full potential. Working in a collaborative and supportive environment, you'll contribute to initiatives that shape the student experience across the University while advancing wellbeing, accessibility and equity outcomes for our diverse community. Your New Role!   As a Learning Accessibility Consultant, you'll play a key role in supporting students with disability and health conditions to succeed throughout their studies at Murdoch University. Working collaboratively with students and staff, you'll champion inclusive teaching practices, support the integration of Universal Design for Learning (UDL) principles, deliver training on accessible technologies and identify appropriate reasonable adjustments that remove barriers to learning. This is an opportunity to combine strategic influence with meaningful student support, helping to create a positive and equitable student experience. Based at our South Street campus, you'll have the option to work from our Mandurah office one day per week. While this is optional, occasional work at the Mandurah campus may be required during semester periods. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Continuous| Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $101K – $133K (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter and a separate statement (5 - 7 pages) addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: A Bachelor's degree in Education with experience supporting students with disability, or a Bachelor's degree in Disability, Allied Health or a related field with experience in accessible learning design or teaching. Knowledge of disability, health and mental health conditions and their impact on learning. Experience applying Universal Design for Learning (UDL) principles in a learning environment. Confidence using educational and accessibility technologies across PC and Mac platforms. Strong relationship-building and change management skills Please note, the successful candidate will be required to have a valid working with children check or the ability to register for one in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Heather Hobert, Manager, Access and Inclusion, heather.hobert@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105833 as the reference. Applications Close on 4 October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Fees-and-Reporting-Officer_JR105857": {
      "title": "Fees and Reporting Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team Join our dynamic Fees and Reporting team and play a vital role in core student administration functions, in collaboration with Admissions, the Enrolments and Progress team, and Completion and Graduations. As a member of our team, you will have the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on a student’s administrative journey. Your New Role!   As a Fees and Reporting Officer, you will play a key role in supporting the University's student fee and reporting functions. Your daily tasks will include fee collection, ensuring compliance with HELP legislation and University requirements, assessing OS-HELP eligibility, evaluating remission of debt applications, and processing refund requests in accordance with the University's Fee Rules. Additionally, you will oversee reporting obligations under the Tertiary Collection of Student Information (TCSI) framework. We are seeking a candidate who can approach sensitive and complex cases with tact, empathy, and sound professional judgement. You will be a decision maker for remission of debt under special circumstances, balancing policy requirements with individual circumstances in a fair and considered manner. This position would suit someone who enjoys variety, is naturally curious, and likes to understand how their work contributes to the bigger picture. The successful candidate will take ownership of tasks, demonstrate strong attention to detail, and proactively follow matters through to achieve the best possible outcomes for students. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Continuous | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $82K – $100K (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic Flexible work arrangements For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Degree with subsequent work experience; or an equivalent combination or relevant experience and/or education/training. Understanding of current regulatory requirements relating to student administration Highly effective communication, customer service and interpersonal skills Experience in administering financial programs including providing ongoing monitoring of compliance with relevant policies and procedures. Analytical and problem-solving skills  Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity, please reach out to Alex Collins, Team Leader Fees and Reporting, at a.collins@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105857 as the reference. Applications Close on 4 October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    }
  },
